President Trump and Russian President  Vladimir Putin have spoken for the first  time since the release of the Muller  report mr. Trump said he and Putin  discussed several matters he says they  briefly talked about the Russia Pro but  mr. Trump said he did not warn Putin not  to meddle in next year's election this  as the democrat-led House Judiciary  Committee has given Attorney General  William Bar a deadline to turn over an  unredacted copy of the Muller report  Steve Dorsey is at the White House with  more Steve good morning Anthony good  morning the call between the two leaders  lasted more than an hour with the  Kremlin signaling mr. Trump and Putin  plan to ramp up dialogue with each other  I had a very good talk with President  Putin following a meeting with Slovakian  Prime Minister Peter Pellegrini in the  Oval Office President Trump  described a warm conversation with  Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin we  talked about many things Venezuela was  one of the topics and he is not looking  at all to get involved in Venezuela but  that's at odds with assessments from his  own administration including Secretary  of State Mike Pompeo who's due to meet  next week with Russian Foreign Minister  Sergey Lavrov at a summit in Finland the  Russians have people working over there  in the hundreds if not more the these  are the folks who are actually  controlling the direction of travel for  Venezuela Pompeyo also says the US won't  rule out military intervention in  Venezuela to aid opposition leader Hwang  Guido it's a move that could threaten to  escalate tensions there with Russia in  his call with Putin the president says  he also indicated he'd be open to an  agreement with Russia and China to  reduce some nuclear firepower the two  also discussed North Korea Ukraine trade  and the Mullah report he actually sort  of smiled when he said something to the  effect that it started off as a mountain  and it ended up being a mouse but he  knew that because he knew there was no  collusion whatsoever but Democrats  aren't smiling on Capitol Hill where  House Judiciary Committee Chairman  Jerrold Nadler issued a new demand  Friday for attorney general bill Barr to  turn  in unredacted Muller report and  underlying materials by Monday at 9:00  a.m. or the committee will move to  contempt proceedings it comes after bar  was a no-show at a house hearing  Thursday after testifying for five hours  to the Senate Judiciary Committee the  day before Democrats accused Barr of  lying to Congress about Robert Muller's  concerns about his initial conclusions  of the report in a Friday letter to  Muller Senate Judiciary Committee  chairman Lindsey Graham asked him if he  felt Barr misrepresented their telephone  conversation and his Senate testimony  this week meanwhile it appears unlikely  the president will allow former White  House lawyer Don McGann to testify to  lawmakers about him disobeying in order  to remove Muller as special counsel  tarika Thank You Steve Dorsey at the  White House
 

